IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc31-forms-process.l4 -- Forms 28, 29, 29.1, 32, 34, 40 and 41 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46:
-- the endorsements of warrants, the recognizance and its list of conditions, the writ of fieri facias, and the challenges to the array
-- and for cause. Layer 1: the law as the Forms state it, from the text alone, from no one's point of view.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How to read a result (NOTES.md): MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE: the Form's words reach the case. JUST FALSE: the Form says no in its own
-- words (an "if", "while", "until" or "subject to" that fails or is met). NOTHING: not covered (a premise not made out, a limit of the
-- grant, an open list, a seam answer that is not JUST TRUE). A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Seam inputs, named as PLAN.md section 4 and section 7 name them: `s 2 justice: ...` (ccc-definitions), `s 522 ...`, `s 638(1) ...`
-- (the parts that own those sections; found, not given: NOTES.md "Seams").
-- Names begin `form N` so that no name collides with another part's.

§ `Form 28 (Section 528) -- Endorsement of Warrant`

-- src:18518 | FORM 28 (Section 528) Endorsement of Warrant
-- src:18519 | Canada,
-- src:18520 | Province of ,
-- src:18521 | (territorial division).
-- src:18522 | In accordance with the application this day made to me, I authorize the arrest of the accused (or defendant), within the (territorial division).
-- src:18523 | Dated (date), at (place).
-- src:18524 | (Signature of justice)
@ref Form 28 (Section 528) (src:18518-18524)
GIVEN `the endorsement is made in accordance with an application made to the justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 justice: the person who signs the endorsement is a justice` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the arrest is within the territorial division the endorsement names` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 28 the endorsement authorizes the arrest of the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the endorsement is made in accordance with an application made to the justice`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In accordance with the application this day made to me, I authorize the arrest"
        IF NOT (`s 2 justice: the person who signs the endorsement is a justice` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(Signature of justice)": the authorization is a justice's, and what a justice is, s 2, is an input
        IF `the arrest is within the territorial division the endorsement names`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "I authorize the arrest of the accused (or defendant), within the (territorial division)": outside the territorial division the Form is silent

§ `Form 28.1 -- repealed`

-- src:18526 | FORM 28.1
-- src:18527 | [Repealed, 2007, c. 22, s. 26]

§ `Form 29 (Section 507) -- Endorsement of Warrant`

-- src:18529 | FORM 29 (Section 507) Endorsement of Warrant
-- src:18530 | Canada,
-- src:18531 | Province of ,
-- src:18532 | (territorial division).
-- src:18533 | Whereas this warrant is issued under section 507, 508 or 512 of the Criminal Code in respect of an offence other than an offence mentioned in section 522 of the Criminal Code, I hereby authorize the release of the accused pursuant to section 499 of that Act.
-- src:18534 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18535 | A Justice of the Peace in and for
@ref Form 29 (Section 507) (src:18529-18535)
GIVEN `the section under which the warrant is issued` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `s 522 the offence is mentioned in section 522` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 29 the endorsement authorizes the release of the accused under section 499` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the section under which the warrant is issued`'s `section` EQUALS 507
                OR  `the section under which the warrant is issued`'s `section` EQUALS 508
                OR  `the section under which the warrant is issued`'s `section` EQUALS 512)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Whereas this warrant is issued under section 507, 508 or 512 of the Criminal Code"
        IF `s 522 the offence is mentioned in section 522` EQUALS JUST FALSE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "in respect of an offence other than an offence mentioned in section 522": an offence mentioned in s 522 is outside the Form (fork F17), and the answer of s 522 is an input

§ `Form 29.1 (Subsection 705(4)) -- Endorsement of Witness -- Warrant`

-- src:18537 | FORM 29.1 (Subsection 705(4)) Endorsement of Witness — Warrant
-- src:18538 | Canada,
-- src:18539 | Province of ,
-- src:18540 | (territorial division).
-- src:18541 | Whereas this warrant is issued under subsection 705(1) or (2) of the Criminal Code in respect of a witness who has been served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding or who has been bound by a recognizance to attend and give evidence in a proceeding, I authorize the release of that person under subsections 705(4) and (5) of that Act.
-- src:18542 | This endorsement is subject to the following conditions: (specify conditions).
-- src:18543 | Dated (date), at (place)
-- src:18544 | (Signature of judge, justice or provincial court judge)
@ref Form 29.1 (Subsection 705(4)) (src:18537-18544)
GIVEN `the section and subsection under which the warrant is issued` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person has been served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been bound by a recognizance to attend and give evidence in a proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person complies with the conditions the endorsement specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 29.1 the endorsement authorizes the release of the witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (    `the section and subsection under which the warrant is issued`'s `section` EQUALS 705
                AND (   `the section and subsection under which the warrant is issued`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)"
                     OR `the section and subsection under which the warrant is issued`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Whereas this warrant is issued under subsection 705(1) or (2) of the Criminal Code"
        IF NOT (`the person has been served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding` OR `the person has been bound by a recognizance to attend and give evidence in a proceeding`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a witness who has been served with a subpoena to give evidence in a proceeding or who has been bound by a recognizance"
        IF NOT `the person complies with the conditions the endorsement specifies`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This endorsement is subject to the following conditions"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 32 -- Recognizance`

-- src:18566 | FORM 32 (Sections 2, 462.34, 490.9, 550, 683, 706, 707, 779, 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.1, 810.2, 817 and 832) Recognizance
-- src:18567 | Canada,
-- src:18568 | Province of
-- src:18569 | (territorial division)
-- src:18570 | 1 Identification
-- src:18571 | Surname: Given name(s):
-- src:18572 | Date of birth:
-- src:18573 | Home address:
-- src:18574 | Phone number(s): (primary) (other)
-- src:18575 | Other contact information (if any):
-- src:18576 | Employment or Occupation (if any):
-- src:18577 | Name and contact information of employer (if any):
-- src:18578 | 2 Financial Promise or Deposit
-- src:18579 | Pursuant to (provision) of the Criminal Code, I agree to (promise or deposit) the amount of $ , or the other valuable security described here:
-- src:18580 | I understand that if I fail to comply with any of the conditions listed below, this amount or security may be forfeited.
-- src:18581 | 3 Conditions
-- src:18582 | (List the conditions that have been ordered by the court and indicate the duration for which each condition remains in effect.)
-- src:18583 | 4 Variation
-- src:18584 | I understand that I may apply to a judge or a justice of the peace to have any condition in this form cancelled or varied.
-- src:18585 | 5 Conditions in effect
-- src:18586 | I understand that the conditions in this recognizance remain in effect until they are cancelled or changed or until I have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court (sections 763 and 764 of the Criminal Code).
-- src:18587 | 6 Signatures
-- src:18588 | PERSON WHO IS GIVING RECOGNIZANCE:
-- src:18589 | I understand the contents of this form and agree to comply with the conditions that are listed above.
-- src:18590 | Signed on (date), at (place).
-- src:18591 | (Signature of the person)
-- src:18592 | (Print name)
-- src:18593 | SURETY (if applicable):
-- src:18594 | I understand my role and my responsibilities under this recognizance and I agree to act as a surety.
-- src:18595 | I agree to (promise or deposit) as security to the court the amount of $
-- src:18596 | I understand that if the person who is giving this recognizance fails to comply with any of the conditions in this recognizance, the money that I have promised or deposited may be forfeited.
-- src:18597 | Surety Declaration (if applicable)
-- src:18598 | □ Surety Declaration attached. (Section 515.1 of the Criminal Code.)
-- src:18599 | □ Surety excepted from providing Surety Declaration. (Subsection 515.1(2) of the Criminal Code.)
-- src:18600 | Signed on (date), at (place).
-- src:18601 | (Signature of the Surety)
-- src:18602 | (Print name)
-- src:18603 | JUDGE, PROVINCIAL COURT JUDGE, JUSTICE OR CLERK OF THE COURT:
-- src:18604 | Signed on (date), at (place).
-- src:18605 | (Signature of the judge, provincial court judge, justice or clerk of the court)
-- src:18606 | (Print name)
-- src:18607 | List of Conditions
-- src:18608 | (a) has a surety (sections 462.34, 490.9, 550, 779, 810, 817 and 832 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18609 | (b) agrees to keep the peace and be of good behaviour (sections 83.3, 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18610 | (c) abstains from possessing a firearm, crossbow, prohibited weapon, restricted weapon, prohibited device, firearm part, ammunition, prohibited ammunition or explosive substance and surrenders those in their possession and surrenders any authorization, licence or registration certificate or other document enabling the acquisition or possession of a firearm (sections 83.3, 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18611 | (d) participates in a treatment program (sections 810.01, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18612 | (e) wears an electronic monitoring device (if the Attorney General makes the request) (sections 810.01, 810.1 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18613 | (e.1) wears an electronic monitoring device (if the Attorney General has consented to this condition) (section 810.03 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18614 | (e.2) abstains from communicating, directly or indirectly, with the intimate partner, a child of the intimate partner or of the defendant or any relative or close friend of the intimate partner, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary (section 810.03 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18615 | (f) remains within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave that area is obtained from the judge or justice (sections 810.01, 810.03 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18616 | (f.1) refrain from going to any specified place or being within a specified distance of any specified place, except in accordance with any specified conditions that the justice considers necessary (section 810.03 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18617 | (g) returns to and remains at their place of residence at specified times (sections 810.01, 810.1 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18618 | (h) abstains from the consumption of drugs, except in accordance with a medical prescription (sections 810.01, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18619 | (i) abstains from the consumption of alcohol or of any other intoxicating substance, except in accordance with a medical prescription (sections 810.01, 810.03, 810.1 and 810.2 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18620 | (j) abstains from any contact — including communicating by any means — with a person under the age of 18 years, unless doing so under the supervision of a person whom the judge considers appropriate (section 810.1 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18621 | (k) abstains from using the Internet or other digital network, unless doing so in accordance with conditions set by the judge (section 810.1 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18622 | (l) abstains from attending a public park or public swimming area where persons under the age of 18 years are present or can reasonably be expected to be present, or a daycare centre, schoolground or playground (section 810.1 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18623 | (m) appears personally or by counsel at the sittings of the appeal court at which the appeal is to be heard (sections 817 and 832 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18624 | (n) appears in court as required (sections 550, 706 and 707 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18625 | (o) in the case where a warrant was issued under section 462.32 of the Criminal Code or a restraint order was made under subsection 462.33(3) of that Act in relation to any property (set out a description of the property and its location), refrains from doing or causing anything to be done that would result, directly or indirectly, in the disappearance, dissipation or reduction in value of the property or otherwise affect the property so that all or a part thereof could not be subject to an order of forfeiture under section 462.37 or 462.38 of that Act or any other provision of that Act or any other Act of Parliament (section 462.34 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18626 | (p) agrees to prosecute the writ of certiorari at their own expense, without wilful delay, and, if ordered, to pay to the person in whose favour the conviction, order or other proceeding is affirmed their full costs and charges to be taxed according to the practice of the court where the conviction, order or proceeding is affirmed (section 779 of the Criminal Code);
-- src:18627 | (q) any other reasonable conditions, including:
-- src:18628 | – reports at specified times to peace officer or other person designated;
-- src:18629 | – remains within designated territorial jurisdiction;
-- src:18630 | – notifies peace officer or other person designated of any change in their address, employment or occupation;
-- src:18631 | – abstains from communicating, directly or indirectly, with victim, witness or other specified person except in accordance with conditions specified by judge, provincial court judge or justice; and
-- src:18632 | – deposits all their passports as the judge, provincial court judge or justice directs.
@ref Form 32 (Sections 2, 462.34, 490.9, 550, 683, 706, 707, 779, 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.1, 810.2, 817 and 832) (src:18566-18632)
DECLARE `form 32 the surety declaration box` IS ONE OF
    `form 32 surety declaration attached (section 515.1)`
    `form 32 surety excepted from providing a surety declaration (subsection 515.1(2))`

-- Part 2: "I understand that if I fail to comply with any of the conditions listed below, this amount or security may be forfeited."
-- JUST TRUE is the Form's "may be forfeited" (a liability, not a certainty). Fork F4: a failed "if" under a "may" is NOTHING (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12).
@ref Form 32 part 2 (src:18580)
GIVEN `the person has failed to comply with a condition listed in the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 32 part 2 the amount or security may be forfeited` MEANS
    IF `the person has failed to comply with a condition listed in the recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if I fail to comply with any of the conditions listed below, this amount or security may be forfeited"

-- Part 3: "(List the conditions that have been ordered by the court and indicate the duration for which each condition remains in effect.)"
-- Fork F5: a bare "must" not done answers JUST FALSE (the duty is not met); the other reading answers NOTHING.
@ref Form 32 part 3 (src:18581-18582)
GIVEN `the court ordered a condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recognizance lists the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recognizance indicates the duration for which the condition remains in effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 32 part 3 the recognizance lists the conditions ordered and the duration of each` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the court ordered a condition`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Form says what to list of "the conditions that have been ordered by the court", and nothing where none was ordered
        IF `the recognizance lists the condition` AND `the recognizance indicates the duration for which the condition remains in effect`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "List the conditions that have been ordered by the court and indicate the duration for which each condition remains in effect" (a bare "must" not done: fork F5)

-- Part 4: "I understand that I may apply to a judge or a justice of the peace to have any condition in this form cancelled or varied."
@ref Form 32 part 4 (src:18583-18584)
GIVEN `the condition is in the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is to a judge or a justice of the peace` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 32 part 4 the person may apply to cancel or vary a condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the condition is in the recognizance`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any condition in this form"
        IF NOT `the application is to a judge or a justice of the peace`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to a judge or a justice of the peace"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Part 5: the conditions remain in effect "until they are cancelled or changed or until I have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise
-- detained by the court (sections 763 and 764)". The "until" bar of the ruling of 2026-11-05: JUST TRUE before the end event, JUST FALSE
-- after; never "the conditions have ended". Fork F6.
@ref Form 32 part 5 (src:18585-18586)
GIVEN `the conditions have been cancelled or changed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been otherwise detained by the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 32 part 5 the conditions remain in effect` MEANS
    IF     `the conditions have been cancelled or changed`
        OR `the person has been discharged`
        OR `the person has been sentenced`
        OR `the person has been otherwise detained by the court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until they are cancelled or changed or until I have been discharged, sentenced or otherwise detained by the court"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- Part 6, the person giving the recognizance: "I understand the contents of this form and agree to comply with the conditions that are
-- listed above." The duty is the signatory's; it is a duty to comply with a condition listed.
@ref Form 32 part 6 (src:18588-18590)
GIVEN `the person has signed the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition is listed in the recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 32 part 6 the person must comply with the condition` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person has signed the recognizance`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "PERSON WHO IS GIVING RECOGNIZANCE: I understand the contents of this form and agree to comply": the agreement is the signatory's
        IF `the condition is listed in the recognizance`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the conditions that are listed above"

-- Part 6, the surety: "I understand that if the person who is giving this recognizance fails to comply with any of the conditions in this
-- recognizance, the money that I have promised or deposited may be forfeited." Fork F20.
@ref Form 32 part 6 (src:18596)
GIVEN `the person who gave the recognizance has failed to comply with a condition in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 32 part 6 the money the surety has promised or deposited may be forfeited` MEANS
    IF `the person who gave the recognizance has failed to comply with a condition in it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person who is giving this recognizance fails to comply with any of the conditions in this recognizance, the money that I have promised or deposited may be forfeited"

-- Part 6, the Surety Declaration: attached (section 515.1) or the surety excepted (subsection 515.1(2)), "if applicable".
@ref Form 32 part 6 (src:18597-18599)
GIVEN `the recognizance has a surety` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a surety declaration is attached` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surety is excepted from providing a surety declaration under subsection 515.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE OF `form 32 the surety declaration box`
`form 32 part 6 the surety declaration box that applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the recognizance has a surety`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Surety Declaration (if applicable)"
        IF `a surety declaration is attached` AND NOT `the surety is excepted from providing a surety declaration under subsection 515.1(2)`
            THEN JUST `form 32 surety declaration attached (section 515.1)`
        IF `the surety is excepted from providing a surety declaration under subsection 515.1(2)` AND NOT `a surety declaration is attached`
            THEN JUST `form 32 surety excepted from providing a surety declaration (subsection 515.1(2))`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Form offers two boxes and says nothing of both ticked or neither

-- The List of Conditions: one constructor per paragraph (a) to (p) and per entry of (q); the table gives the sections each is listed for.
DECLARE `form 32 the condition in the List of Conditions` IS ONE OF
    `form 32 condition (a) has a surety`
    `form 32 condition (b) agrees to keep the peace and be of good behaviour`
    `form 32 condition (c) abstains from possessing a firearm and the other things listed, and surrenders them and the documents`
    `form 32 condition (d) participates in a treatment program`
    `form 32 condition (e) wears an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request`
    `form 32 condition (e.1) wears an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General has consented to this condition`
    `form 32 condition (e.2) abstains from communicating with the intimate partner and others, except as the justice considers necessary`
    `form 32 condition (f) remains within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave is obtained`
    `form 32 condition (f.1) refrains from going to any specified place, except as the justice considers necessary`
    `form 32 condition (g) returns to and remains at their place of residence at specified times`
    `form 32 condition (h) abstains from the consumption of drugs, except in accordance with a medical prescription`
    `form 32 condition (i) abstains from the consumption of alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, except in accordance with a medical prescription`
    `form 32 condition (j) abstains from any contact with a person under the age of 18 years`
    `form 32 condition (k) abstains from using the Internet or other digital network`
    `form 32 condition (l) abstains from attending a public park or public swimming area, daycare centre, schoolground or playground`
    `form 32 condition (m) appears personally or by counsel at the sittings of the appeal court`
    `form 32 condition (n) appears in court as required`
    `form 32 condition (o) refrains from affecting property under a warrant or restraint order`
    `form 32 condition (p) agrees to prosecute the writ of certiorari at their own expense`
    `form 32 condition (q) any other reasonable conditions`
    `form 32 condition (q) reports at specified times to a peace officer or other person designated`
    `form 32 condition (q) remains within designated territorial jurisdiction`
    `form 32 condition (q) notifies a peace officer or other person designated of any change of address, employment or occupation`
    `form 32 condition (q) abstains from communicating with a victim, witness or other specified person`
    `form 32 condition (q) deposits all their passports`

-- The sections each condition is listed for, as the Form's parentheses give them. The entries of (q) name no section.
@ref Form 32 List of Conditions (src:18608-18632)
GIVEN condition IS A `form 32 the condition in the List of Conditions`
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`form 32 the sections the condition is listed for` MEANS
    CONSIDER condition
    WHEN `form 32 condition (a) has a surety` THEN LIST 462.34, 490.9, 550, 779, 810, 817, 832
    WHEN `form 32 condition (b) agrees to keep the peace and be of good behaviour` THEN LIST 83.3, 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.1, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (c) abstains from possessing a firearm and the other things listed, and surrenders them and the documents` THEN LIST 83.3, 810, 810.01, 810.03, 810.1, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (d) participates in a treatment program` THEN LIST 810.01, 810.03, 810.1, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (e) wears an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General makes the request` THEN LIST 810.01, 810.1, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (e.1) wears an electronic monitoring device, if the Attorney General has consented to this condition` THEN LIST 810.03
    WHEN `form 32 condition (e.2) abstains from communicating with the intimate partner and others, except as the justice considers necessary` THEN LIST 810.03
    WHEN `form 32 condition (f) remains within a specified geographic area unless written permission to leave is obtained` THEN LIST 810.01, 810.03, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (f.1) refrains from going to any specified place, except as the justice considers necessary` THEN LIST 810.03
    WHEN `form 32 condition (g) returns to and remains at their place of residence at specified times` THEN LIST 810.01, 810.1, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (h) abstains from the consumption of drugs, except in accordance with a medical prescription` THEN LIST 810.01, 810.03, 810.1, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (i) abstains from the consumption of alcohol or any other intoxicating substance, except in accordance with a medical prescription` THEN LIST 810.01, 810.03, 810.1, 810.2
    WHEN `form 32 condition (j) abstains from any contact with a person under the age of 18 years` THEN LIST 810.1
    WHEN `form 32 condition (k) abstains from using the Internet or other digital network` THEN LIST 810.1
    WHEN `form 32 condition (l) abstains from attending a public park or public swimming area, daycare centre, schoolground or playground` THEN LIST 810.1
    WHEN `form 32 condition (m) appears personally or by counsel at the sittings of the appeal court` THEN LIST 817, 832
    WHEN `form 32 condition (n) appears in court as required` THEN LIST 550, 706, 707
    WHEN `form 32 condition (o) refrains from affecting property under a warrant or restraint order` THEN LIST 462.34
    WHEN `form 32 condition (p) agrees to prosecute the writ of certiorari at their own expense` THEN LIST 779
    OTHERWISE EMPTY

-- Is the condition one the Form lists for the section? JUST TRUE where the Form lists it for that section. Otherwise NOTHING: the
-- parentheses list the sections without "only" (fork F7), and (q), "any other reasonable conditions, including", names none.
@ref Form 32 List of Conditions (src:18607-18632)
GIVEN condition IS A `form 32 the condition in the List of Conditions`
      section IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 32 the condition is listed for the section` MEANS
    IF elem (section's `section`) (`form 32 the sections the condition is listed for` condition)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the sections in the parentheses after the condition are listed and the list is not closed with "only"; (q) "any other reasonable conditions, including:" names no section

§ `Form 34 (Section 771) -- Writ of Fieri Facias`

-- src:18642 | FORM 34 (Section 771) Writ of Fieri Facias
-- src:18643 | Elizabeth II by the Grace of God, etc.
-- src:18644 | To the sheriff of (territorial division), GREETING.
-- src:18645 | You are hereby commanded to levy of the goods and chattels, lands and tenements of each of the following persons the amount set opposite the name of each:
-- src:18646 | Name Address Occupation Amount
-- src:18647 | And you are further commanded to make a return of what you have done in execution of this writ.
-- src:18648 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18649 | Clerk of the
-- src:18650 | (Seal)
@ref Form 34 (Section 771) (src:18642-18650)
DECLARE `form 34 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 34 levy the amount from the person's goods and chattels, lands and tenements`
    `form 34 make a return of what the sheriff has done in execution of the writ`

-- "You are hereby commanded to levy of the goods and chattels, lands and tenements of each of the following persons the amount set opposite
-- the name of each": the amount still to be levied from a person named in the writ. A person not named: not covered.
@ref Form 34 (Section 771) (src:18645-18646)
GIVEN `the person is named in the writ` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount set opposite the person's name` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount already levied from the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`form 34 the amount the sheriff is commanded to levy from the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person is named in the writ`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each of the following persons the amount set opposite the name of each"
        IF `the amount already levied from the person` AT LEAST `the amount set opposite the person's name`
            THEN JUST 0
        OTHERWISE JUST (`the amount set opposite the person's name` MINUS `the amount already levied from the person`)

-- "And you are further commanded to make a return of what you have done in execution of this writ."
@ref Form 34 (Section 771) (src:18647)
GIVEN `the person is the sheriff to whom the writ is addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 34 the sheriff is commanded to make a return` MEANS
    IF `the person is the sheriff to whom the writ is addressed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "To the sheriff of (territorial division), GREETING. ... you are further commanded to make a return"

-- The two commands as a regulative rule. The sheriff is a peace officer under paragraph (a) of the definition in s 2 (NEEDS-CORE.md).
@ref Form 34 (Section 771) (src:18645-18647)
`form 34 the duties of the sheriff` MEANS
    PARTY `a peace officer`
    MUST `form 34 levy the amount from the person's goods and chattels, lands and tenements`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `a peace officer`
        MUST `form 34 make a return of what the sheriff has done in execution of the writ`
        HENCE FULFILLED
    )

§ `Form 40 (Section 629) -- Challenge To Array`

-- src:18800 | FORM 40 (Section 629) Challenge To Array
-- src:18801 | Canada,
-- src:18802 | Province of ,
-- src:18803 | (territorial division).
-- src:18804 | The Queen
-- src:18805 | v.
-- src:18806 | C.D.
-- src:18807 | The (prosecutor or accused) challenges the array of the panel on the ground that X.Y., (sheriff or deputy sheriff), who returned the panel, was guilty of (partiality or fraud or wilful misconduct) on returning it.
-- src:18808 | Dated this day of A.D. , at .
-- src:18809 | Counsel for (prosecutor or accused)
@ref Form 40 (Section 629) (src:18800-18809)
DECLARE `form 40 who challenges` IS ONE OF
    `form 40 the prosecutor`
    `form 40 the accused`
    `form 40 another person`

DECLARE `form 40 the ground` IS ONE OF
    `form 40 partiality`
    `form 40 fraud`
    `form 40 wilful misconduct`
    `form 40 another ground`

@ref Form 40 (Section 629) (src:18807)
GIVEN challenger IS A `form 40 who challenges`
      `the person who returned the panel is a sheriff or deputy sheriff` IS A BOOLEAN
      ground IS A `form 40 the ground`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 40 the challenge to the array is in the Form's terms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF challenger EQUALS `form 40 another person`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The (prosecutor or accused) challenges the array"
        IF NOT `the person who returned the panel is a sheriff or deputy sheriff`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "X.Y., (sheriff or deputy sheriff), who returned the panel"
        IF ground EQUALS `form 40 another ground`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "was guilty of (partiality or fraud or wilful misconduct) on returning it": the three are alternatives to fill in, not a list closed with "only"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 41 (Section 639) -- Challenge for Cause`

-- src:18811 | FORM 41 (Section 639) Challenge for Cause
-- src:18812 | Canada,
-- src:18813 | Province of ,
-- src:18814 | (territorial division).
-- src:18815 | The Queen
-- src:18816 | v.
-- src:18817 | C.D.
-- src:18818 | The (prosecutor or accused) challenges G.H. on the ground that (set out ground of challenge in accordance with subsection 638(1) of theCriminal Code ).
-- src:18819 | Counsel for (prosecutor or accused)
@ref Form 41 (Section 639) (src:18811-18819)
DECLARE `form 41 who challenges` IS ONE OF
    `form 41 the prosecutor`
    `form 41 the accused`
    `form 41 another person`

-- "(set out ground of challenge in accordance with subsection 638(1) of the Criminal Code)": whether the ground is one of subsection 638(1)
-- is an input (the part that owns s 638). Fork F9: a ground the seam says is not one of 638(1) is NOTHING here (the Form's direction is not
-- itself a "no"); the other reading is JUST FALSE.
@ref Form 41 (Section 639) (src:18818)
GIVEN challenger IS A `form 41 who challenges`
      `s 638(1) the ground is a ground of challenge under subsection 638(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 41 the challenge for cause is in the Form's terms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF challenger EQUALS `form 41 another person`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The (prosecutor or accused) challenges"
        IF `s 638(1) the ground is a ground of challenge under subsection 638(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "set out ground of challenge in accordance with subsection 638(1)": the answer of s 638(1) is an input (fork F9)
